.TH HALCYON-ISLANDS 1 "October 2026" "Halcyon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
halcyon-islands \- activate the optional Islands panel for one user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halcyon-islands
.RI "{status|enable|disable}"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Islands panel splits the COSMIC panel into floating islands. Turning it on
is optional and takes effect the next time you sign in. Run this command as
your desktop user.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report installation, selector compatibility and per-user activation state.
.TP
.B enable
Install the packaged companion into your home and turn it on for the next sign-in.
Unsupported or unreadable COSMIC package versions and a recorded Islands failure
refuse activation without replacing the per-user companion. Version mismatches
report installed and supported builds. A later COSMIC update that does not match
selects the normal panel automatically.
.TP
.B disable
Restore this command's installations. Sign out and back in to use the standard panel.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means success. For status, 0 requires an installed, compatible and enabled
companion, including one waiting for the next sign-in. 1 means an unavailable or
disabled companion, or an operation failed. 2 means invalid usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/cosmic-ext-halcyon-islands/README
Supported versions, activation prerequisites, recovery and removal instructions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cosmic-desktop-cards/companion
Per-user companion bundle.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cosmic-desktop-cards/backups
Installation journals and backups retained for restoration.
.SH NOTES
No running panel is restarted. Disable for every user before removing the
package. Previous source installations must be restored before enabling here.

.SH SOURCE QUALIFICATION
New companion builds accept distribution rebuilds of reviewed source triples
when the native ABI and compositor preflight succeeds. Unknown source revisions
and mixed triples select the standard panel. A COSMIC release number alone is not a guarantee.
Status reports static eligibility; startup performs the runtime checks.
